# build
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.rsuser
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# test and coverage output
TestResults/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml

# logs from a failed build
msbuild.log
msbuild.err
msbuild.wrn

# local config and secrets
.env

# Run profiles are where a connection string with a token ends up, because it is the
# fastest way to make F5 work. Same treatment as .env: the real file stays out, and a
# launchSettings.example.json carries the variable names when one is needed.
# User secrets live in %APPDATA%\Microsoft\UserSecrets and never reach the tree, which is
# why UserSecretsId in the csproj is safe to commit.
Properties/launchSettings.json
**/Properties/launchSettings.json

# generated
graphify-out/

# left by the installer
*.bak-*

# per-developer Claude settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# written by the session hook, one file per machine
.claude/session-state.json

# Working papers between a human and an agent: plans, handover briefs and their
# attachments. They are written to be acted on and then to go stale, and a stale plan in a
# repository reads as a description of the code. What survives them belongs in DECISIONS.md
# (why a thing is the way it is) or in docs/ as a measurement (what was observed).
docs/plans/
docs/attachments/
docs/*-brief.md
